NXR-159|Optional portable DMA staging and quarantine implementation|DMA|An optional DMA module shall serialize thread callers over one active transfer per channel using boot-reserved exclusive staging and explicit BSP address/cache/quiescence contracts, without retaining application-buffer pointers.|Unknown hardware stop semantics must not expose temporary caller storage to late DMA or force DMA storage into the nano kernel.|DMA defaults off and adds no kernel fields; TX copies before launch; RX copies only after quiescent completion; stale tickets cannot release new transfers; uncertain abort quarantines until positive stop proof; host ownership tests pass.|Enabled host ownership model, memory tooling, cross-compilation and disabled-image size/symbol checks.|NXR-133,NXR-134,NXR-135|RTOS_DMA requires RTOS_SYNC; nexrt::dma is a separate library; polled BSP interface rather than assumed external IRQ support.|Per explicitly instantiated channel control plus caller-selected aligned permanent staging; no heap, mandatory worker, descriptor ring or global pool.|include/rtos_dma.hpp,src/dma.cpp,cmake/modules.cmake,cmake/configuration.cmake,docs/dma.rst,docs/drivers.rst|Portable channel layer implemented; concrete FPGA/PCIe engine, interrupt dispatch, cache operations and physical DMA qualification remain BSP work. Earlier hardware DMA roadmap requirements are not marked complete.|include/rtos_dma.hpp,src/dma.cpp,cmake/modules.cmake,cmake/configuration.cmake|tests/dma.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
